    "lines": [
      {
        "scene": "hook",
        "text": "Markets are falling. Time to stop my SIP, right?",
        "start": 0.27,
        "seconds": 2.57,
        "window": 2.97,
        "fill": 0.865
      },
      {
        "scene": "headline",
        "text": "Look at the data. In September, Indians put a record ₹32,490 Cr into SIPs.",
        "start": 3.23,
        "seconds": 6.08,
        "window": 6.7,
        "fill": 0.907
      },
      {
        "scene": "why",
        "text": "Because a SIP is built for falls. The same amount buys more units when prices are low.",
        "start": 9.93,
        "seconds": 4.92,
        "window": 5.5,
        "fill": 0.895
      },
      {
        "scene": "plan",
        "text": "Take ₹5,000 a month for 15 years. You put in ₹9.0 L.",
        "start": 15.43,
        "seconds": 3.9,
        "window": 4.53,
        "fill": 0.861
      },
      {
        "scene": "grow",
        "text": "At an assumed 12% a year, it could grow to ₹25.2 L. But only if the payments keep coming.",
        "start": 19.97,
        "seconds": 6.21,
        "window": 6.83,
        "fill": 0.909
      },
      {
        "scene": "sharma",
        "text": "I have seen many falls. The habit lasts longer than the fear.",
        "start": 26.8,
        "seconds": 2.84,
        "window": 3.43,
        "fill": 0.828
      },
      {
        "scene": "lesson",
        "text": "Falls feel scary. But for a monthly investor, they also mean cheaper units.",
        "start": 30.23,
        "seconds": 3.76,
        "window": 4.4,
        "fill": 0.855
      },
      {
        "scene": "outro",
        "text": "So, did yours keep going?",
        "start": 34.63,
        "seconds": 1.27,
        "window": 1.8,
        "fill": 0.706
      }
